cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this result table or code, please cite it as below."
title: "Home or Abroad? Where Elite Player Exposure Adds Information About Future National-Team Strength"
abstract: >-
  A forecasting study of elite player exposure and future national-team match
  strength, prepared for the MIT Sloan Sports Analytics Conference (Soccer
  track, Problem 14). Domestic and abroad elite playing minutes are tested
  against a lagged Elo outcome across five big-five federations (2012-2025)
  and an expanded 90-federation panel (1,216 team-season rows). Elo is treated
  as a lagged match-result outcome rather than ground truth for national-team
  quality. All findings are predictive associations, not causal effects.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-28
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/RupayanHalder39/MITSloanProblem14-home-or-abroad-player-exposure"
url: "https://github.com/RupayanHalder39/MITSloanProblem14-home-or-abroad-player-exposure"
keywords:
  - association football
  - Elo ratings
  - forecasting
  - player development
  - sports analytics
  - MIT Sloan Sports Analytics Conference

